][<SPT><TTL>Transformer Differential Relays (MFR4)</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Provide high-speed, microprocessor based transformer differential relays.  Relays must be configurable for single-phase and three-phase protection.  
Bus configurations having more than 6 terminals require additional relays to protect all busses.  The relays must utilize mirrored bits communications 
for transfer trip functions.</TXT><BRK/>
<OLG><BRK/>
<OLI>Product Description:  <RID>IEEE C37.90</RID> Microprocessor-based bus differential protection relay, IEEE Device number 87B.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI>Mounting:  Flush mounted device, installed on<MET> 480 mm</MET><ENG> 19 inch</ENG> mounting plates for<MET> 480 mm</MET><ENG> 19 inch</ENG> equipment rack.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI>Output Contacts:  Provide output contacts rated for 30 amperes making current, 6 amperes continuous current at 70 degrees C.  Contacts must not be rated less than 48 volts DC.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Provide one contact to trip lock-out relay on bus differential trip function. Wire test switch in series with this output contact.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Provide multiple contacts to function as back-up overcurrent protective devices (IEEE 50/51) for sources and loads on protected 
bus.  Circuit breakers on protected bus must have their own output contacts and relay test switches.  Wire test switch in 
series with output contacts.  Refer to PROTECTIVE RELAY AND METERING TEST SWITCHES in this Section.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI>Alarm Contact:  Provide alarm contact wired in series with relay test switch.  Wire alarm to signal supervisory control and data acquisition 
system (SCADA) upon following conditions.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Current transformer open.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Relay failure.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Battery voltage monitor.  Provide dual level substation battery voltage monitor with following adjustable parameters.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="3">Low level warning adjustable from 15 to 300 volts DC.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="3">High level warning adjustable from 15 to 300 volts DC.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="3">Low level failure adjustable from 15 to 300 volts DC.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="3">High level failure adjustable from 15 to 300 volts DC.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="3">Peak to peak AC ripple detection adjustable from 1 to 300 volts AC.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="3">Substation battery ground detection, adjustable.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI>Control and Status Inputs:</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Provide status input of lockout relay and wire to indicate trip condition.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Provide status input from contact on circuit breakers on protected bus.  Contacts must be open when breaker is OPEN and 
closed when breaker is CLOSED.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI>Current Inputs:  Provide individual inputs from current transformers for circuit breakers on protected buses.  Route current from current 
transformers to shorting terminal blocks, from shorting terminal blocks to shorting relay test switches, and from test switches to relay.  
Paralleling current transformers is prohibited. Current input ratings must be as follows.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Nominal current must be 5 amperes to match current transformer secondary ratings.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Continuous current must be 15 amperes, linear to 100 amperes symmetrical.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Burden must not exceed 0.30 VA at 5 amperes and 3.0 VA at 15 amperes.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI>Protective Functions:</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Six or more low-impedance current differential circuits per phase (zone of protection).</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Relay must have high sensitivity for internal faults and low sensitivity for external faults.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Open and short circuit current transformer detection and alarm.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Breaker failure detection.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Instantaneous overcurrent protection (Device 50) for protected circuit breakers.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Time-overcurrent protection (Device 51) for protected circuit breakers.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">End-zone protection for faults between open circuit breaker and CT.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI>IRIG-B.  The relay must include an interface port for a demodulated IRIG-B time synchronization input signal.  The relays must
 generate a time synchronizing signal to provide a synchronizing signal to other relays.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI>Communications Protocols:  The relay must come equipped with following protocols, whether used by application or not.  Refer to SUPERVISORY 
CONTROL AND DATA ACQUISITION (SCADA) of this Section for supervisory, control, and data acquisition requirements.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Protocols must include ASCII, Compressed ASCII, DNP3.0, <RID>IEC 61850</RID>, Telnet, FTP, and Mirrored Bits.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Digital Relay-to-Relay Communications.  The relay must include send and receive logic elements and provide analog and virtual 
terminal service in two communications ports for dedicated relay-to-relay communication.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2"><RID>IEC 61850</RID> Ethernet Communications.  The relay must provide <RID>IEC 61850</RID>-compliant communications.  The <RID>IEC 61850</RID> capability must include GOOSE messaging and defined logical node data points.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI>Communications Ports:  Provide ports as follows.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Front <RID>TIA-232</RID> serial port for uploading and downloading settings, event reports, and data via laptop computer.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Port 1 must be serial <RID>TIA-232</RID> port supporting SEL ASCII, Compressed ASCII, and Settings File Transfer, SEL Fast Meter with 
Configuration, Fast Operate, Fast SER, Enhanced MIRRORED BITS Communications, and DNP3 Level 2 Slave Plus Dial-out.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Port 2 must be serial <RID>TIA-232</RID> port supporting SEL ASCII, Compressed ASCII, and Settings File Transfer, SEL Fast Meter with 
Configuration, Fast Operate, Fast SER, Enhanced MIRRORED BITS Communications, and DNP3 Level 2 Slave Plus Dial-out.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Port 3 must be serial <RID>TIA-232</RID> port supporting SEL ASCII, Compressed ASCII, and Settings File Transfer, SEL Fast Meter with 
Configuration, Fast Operate, Fast SER, Enhanced MIRRORED BITS Communications, and DNP3 Level 2 Slave Plus Dial-out.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Port 4 not used.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Port 5 must be dual redundant 100 Base-FX multimode fiber ports for Ethernet communications.  Ports must operate in 
failover mode.  Ports must support FTP file transfer protocol, <RID>IEC 61850</RID> protocol, <RID>IEC 61850</RID> GOOSE messaging, and DNP 3.0 
protocol with up to three DNP sessions.</OLI><BRK/></OLG>
<BRK/></SPT>
